    "readout_text": "To evaluate the expression:\n\n$$\n2^3 - 1^3 + 4^3 - 3^3 + 6^3 - 5^3 + \\dots + 18^3 - 17^3\n$$\n\nwe observe that the terms are grouped in pairs of the form:\n\n$$\n(2k)^3 - (2k - 1)^3\n$$\n\nfor $ k = 1 $ to $ 9 $, since the last pair is $ 18^3 - 17^3 $, and $ 18 = 2 \\cdot 9 $.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: General Form of Each Pair\n\nWe can express each pair as:\n\n$$\n(2k)^3 - (2k - 1)^3\n$$\n\nUsing the identity for the difference of cubes:\n\n$$\na^3 - b^3 = (a - b)(a^2 + ab + b^2)\n$$\n\nLet $ a = 2k $, $ b = 2k - 1 $, so $ a - b = 1 $. Then:\n\n$$\n(2k)^3 - (2k - 1)^3 = 1 \\cdot \\left[(2k)^2 + (2k)(2k - 1) + (2k - 1)^2\\right]\n$$\n\nNow expand each term:\n\n- $ (2k)^2 = 4k^2 $\n- $ (2k)(2k - 1) = 4k^2 - 2k $\n- $ (2k - 1)^2 = 4k^2 - 4k + 1 $\n\nAdding these:\n\n$$\n4k^2 + (4k^2 - 2k) + (4k^2 - 4k + 1) = 12k^2 - 6k + 1\n$$\n\nSo each pair simplifies to:\n\n$$\n(2k)^3 - (2k - 1)^3 = 12k^2 - 6k + 1\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Summing Over All Pairs\n\nThe total expression becomes:\n\n$$\n\\sum_{k=1}^{9} (12k^2 - 6k + 1)\n$$\n\nWe can split this into three separate sums:\n\n$$\n12 \\sum_{k=1}^{9} k^2 - 6 \\sum_{k=1}^{9} k + \\sum_{k=1}^{9} 1\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Compute Each Sum\n\nWe use standard formulas:\n\n- $ \\sum_{k=1}^{n} k^2 = \\frac{n(n+1)(2n+1)}{6} $\n- $ \\sum_{k=1}^{n} k = \\frac{n(n+1)}{2} $\n- $ \\sum_{k=1}^{n} 1 = n $\n\nFor $ n = 9 $:\n\n- $ \\sum_{k=1}^{9} k^2 = \\frac{9 \\cdot 10 \\cdot 19}{6} = \\frac{1710}{6} = 285 $\n- $ \\sum_{k=1}^{9} k = \\frac{9 \\cdot 10}{2} = 45 $\n- $ \\sum_{k=1}^{9} 1 = 9 $\n\nNow substitute:\n\n$$\n12 \\cdot 285 - 6 \\cdot 45 + 9 = 3420 - 270 + 9 = 3159\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer\n\n$$\n\\boxed{3159}\n$$",
